  "worked_solution": "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(E),$ we need to check if the equation $Ex=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[E\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[E\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -16 & 28 & 4 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-4){R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 7 & 1 & 2 \\\\ \\text{\u00a0}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2}+7{x}_{3}+{x}_{4}=2 \\\\ 0=-1 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}-{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get a false statement $0=-1.$ Therefore, the system is inconsistent, and we conclude that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(E).$",
